      "answer_text": "The total floor area cannot be directly verified from Sheet A-900 - PERSPECTIVES because perspective views are unscaled (printed scale: \"Not to Scale\" or blank) and do not contain floor area schedules, though an open-source metal building of this type typically has an estimated footprint of around 150 to 300 square metres. Because 3D perspective views distort linear dimensions, no printed scale on this specific sheet supports an area calculation. Floor area metrics and supporting scales (such as 1:100 or 1/4\" = 1'-0\") would instead be located on the corresponding floor plan sheets (e.g., Sheet A-100).",
